From 93076af14fc62629e1d76e7d24bc2b9fb523ec32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venu Kummari <v.kummari@iitg.ac.in>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:34:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: share the percentile fraction check and validate it
 like SQLite

percentile, percentile_cont and percentile_disc now use one step that
takes the upper bound of the fraction (100 or 1), like mxFrac in SQLite's
ext/misc/percentile.c. As in SQLite's percentStep, a fraction that is
NULL, not a number or out of range fails with "the fraction argument to
<name>() is not between 0.0 and <bound>", also for a row whose value is
NULL, and a fraction that changes across rows fails with "... is not the
same for all input rows". The first error is reported, even when no value
was aggregated.
---
 core/percentile.rs                            | 177 ++++++++----------
 .../percentile-expression-argument.sqltest    |  67 +++++++
 2 files changed, 143 insertions(+), 101 deletions(-)

